:: OC Zach Brochella Ask Dad [nobr]

/* Cooking */
<<if $BroDadLocation == "Cooking">>
    You watch as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> slaves away cooking dinner for you and your brothers. <span style="color:Yellow">You gulp nervously, trying to build up the courage to ask him about the music festival.</span> You’re not exactly afraid of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span>, but are feeling the nervousness all kids feel just before asking their parents for something they know they normally wouldn’t be allowed to do. It is as you are about to open your mouth that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span>’s voice suddenly causes you to jump. <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Dad",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Smile",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“If you are going to just stand there not saying anything, could you at least help wash up?”</span> You nod, quickly running over to clean up what he’s finished with as you go over how you are going to ask him in your head one more time before finally asking if he’s heard of Brochella-Lite. <br>
    <br>

/* In his Room */
<<elseif $BroDadLocation == "Bedroom">>
    You stand at the doorway of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span>’s bedroom, <span style="color:Yellow">trying to work up the courage to ask him about the music festival.</span> You aren’t exactly afraid of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span>, but are still feeling the nervousness all kids feel just before asking their parents for something they know they normally wouldn’t be allowed to do. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> spots you standing there and, with a smirk, asks <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Alright, what do you want or what did you do?”</span> <br>
    
        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Dad",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Smile",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    You blush, asking him what he’s talking about. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Please. The only reason one of my lovely sons would be standing there looking like that is because he is either in trouble or wants something. I don’t hear any crying or things breaking, so I assume you want something. So come on. The worst I can say is no. Well, maybe I’ll give you a spank if it’s something silly, but just a little one.”</span> Chuckling nervously, you ask him if he’s heard of Brochella-Lite. <br>
    <br>

/* Watching TV */
<<elseif $BroDadLocation == "TV">>
    You stand just behind <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span>, who is sitting in his recliner watching TV. <span style="color:Yellow">You are trying to work up the courage to ask him about the music festival.</span> You aren’t exactly afraid of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span>, but are still feeling the nervousness all kids feel just before asking their parents for something they know they normally wouldn’t be allowed to do. You are just about to finally say something when the voice of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> makes you jump. <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Dad",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Smile",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“What it is, $DadNickname?”</span> You nearly fall back in surprise. Parents really do have eyes on the back of their heads! You think about sneaking away, maybe he was just guessing and hadn’t really seen you, but then he turns around and looks at you with a smirk. It is obvious you want something. So, you take a deep breath and ask him if he’s heard of Brochella-Lite. <br>
    <br>
<</if>>

<<unset $BroDadLocation>>

/* Continued */
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Brochella-Lite…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> looks off into the distance with a smile like people do on TV when a flashback occurs. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Now that brings back some memories. I didn’t even think they still did that! Haha.”</span> He stops what he’s doing and steps over to you, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“You know, Alister, some friends, and I used to sneak out to go to these when we were around your age. The atmosphere is something else. The music, the people, the food. Those were the days!”</span> He sighs in happy remembrance, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Of course, when the folks caught us, it became a very, very bad day. Haha.”</span> He pauses, as if suddenly remember where he was, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“And if you try to sneak out like that, it’ll be a lot worse for you.”</span> <span style="color:Pink">He slaps his wrist, a playful threat of what your rear will be feeling if you try that.</span> <br>
<br>
You blush and blurt out that you would NEVER try something like that. Which is why you are here, actually. You heard about the festival at school and wanted to go check it out. You know it goes late, but you figured this would be a great way experience musical culture and the town and… and he’s always telling you to be more open to new experiences and-! <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Alright, alright.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> laughs, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I’d be a hypocrite if I just banned it outright, but midnight is a little late for a little kid like you to be out by himself.”</span> You blush, you’re not that little. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I’d take you, but I need to be up early Sunday…”</span> He pauses and thinks for a second, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Alright. You can go…”</span> You smile, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“BUT! Only if <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Gabe</span> agrees to go with you.”</span> You frown. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Ah come on, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Gabe</span> loves music. I’m sure he was planning to go anyway. I’m sure he was planning to ask me, if he knows what’s good for him. So, you tell <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Gabe</span> that he can go if he takes you. Think of it as brotherly bonding. And because neither one of you can go without the other.”</span> He smiles, as if he had come up with some great plan. He then pats you on the head before returning to what he was doing, proud of his parenting skills. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:Yellow"> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Gabe</span>… You’re pretty sure this would be up his alley, but whether or not he’d be interested in having to drag his little brother around is another story… <br>
<br>
Well, the only thing you can do is ask.</span> <br>
